Streaming music service Tidal <a href="https://x.com/rsa/status/2125227948890563014">today said</a> it plans to start blocking AI music on December 9. Any track generated entirely with AI will be removed from the platform, with Tidal rejecting AI songs in the future.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/tidal-logo.jpg" alt="" width="1200" height="630" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1079391" /><br/>
Tidal lead Robert Andersen said 43 percent of tracks uploaded in the last 90 days have been flagged as AI-generated. Approximately 29 million songs will be deleted and Tidal expects 80,000 to 85,000 songs to be rejected per day.<br/>
<br/>
AI music will start disappearing on December 9 and will be "completely gone" at the beginning of 2027. AI-assisted music will continue to be allowed, since the policy is only for songs made entirely with AI tools. Tidal previously demonetized AI music, but removing it goes a step further.<br/>
<br/>
Andersen said Tidal believes the move will "resonate with both artists and listeners alike" because 96 percent of AI songs get zero plays.<br/>
<br/>
Apple hasn't banned AI songs from <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-music/">Apple Music</a>, but it introduced <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/03/05/apple-music-ai-transparency-tags/">AI Transparency Tags</a> earlier this year. Apple is relying on labels and distributors to disclose when AI has been used, and it <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/08/20/apple-music-to-label-ai-generated-songs/">said in August</a> that tracks "materially generated using AI" must have a "Made With AI" label.<br/>
<br/>
In April, &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj; VP Oliver Schusser said that more than a third of monthly uploads to &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj; are 100 percent AI-generated, but AI music accounted for less than 0.5 percent of actual listening.<div class="linkback">Tags: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-music/">Apple Music</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/tidal/">Tidal</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/24/tidal-ai-music-ban/">Tidal Bans AI Music, While Apple Music Sticks to Labels</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/tidal-bans-ai-music-while-apple-music-sticks-to-labels.2495175/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>